-- Vortex Pinnacle: the creature templates had melee damage multipliers and levels that do not match the 4.3.4 data and, apart from the three bosses, no
-- link to a heroic copy: the heroic copies of the trash were level 1 friendly placeholders that nothing used, so the heroic dungeon had the stats of the
-- normal one. The trash is linked to its heroic copy, the heroic copies get the 4.3.4 values (level 85) and the heroic copy of a trash type that drops
-- items uses the loot table of its normal entry. The helpers of the dungeon (slipstreams, landing zones, Howling Gale, Zephyr, the triggers) are left as
-- they are. The values come from the 4.3.4 data; flag bits the core does not accept from the database are left out, and the base health curve above
-- level 85 is the Pandaria one, so the rows of level 86 and 87 carry the 4.3.4 health scaled by the ratio of the two curves.
UPDATE `creature_template` SET `maxlevel` = 84, `dmg_multiplier` = 60, `mingold` = 17000, `maxgold` = 23000, `mechanic_immune_mask` = 650854271, `mindmg` = 0, `maxdmg` = 0, `attackpower` = 0 WHERE `entry` = 43873;
